		"comments": [
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a media feature's NAME position takes no number pass: the name is everything\n\tbefore the expression's first colon, so only the value normalizes ",
				"start": 9,
				"end": 158
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " an expression with no colon has no value at all, so its whole interior is name —\n\tthe boolean form and both range forms keep their numbers ",
				"start": 210,
				"end": 354
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a function call in name position is name text like anything else there — and its\n\tparens do not protect the splitting colon, so a name may run INTO a call and the value\n\tstart inside one ",
				"start": 447,
				"end": 639
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " the colon that splits an expression is its first one wherever it sits, so a\n\tgrouped condition's value normalizes ",
				"start": 734,
				"end": 853
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a comment is name text, and the name runs on past it to the colon ",
				"start": 908,
				"end": 979
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " c ",
				"start": 994,
				"end": 1001,
				"position": 6
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a `(` glued to an identifier is a function call in media-type position rather than\n\ta feature expression, so its content takes the number pass like the rest of the type ",
				"start": 1037,
				"end": 1211
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " @custom-media goes through the same reader ",
				"start": 1281,
				"end": 1329
			}
		],
		"content": {
			"start": 7,
			"end": 1357,
			"styles": "\n\t/* a media feature's NAME position takes no number pass: the name is everything\n\tbefore the expression's first colon, so only the value normalizes */\n\t@media (1.50: 2.5) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* an expression with no colon has no value at all, so its whole interior is name —\n\tthe boolean form and both range forms keep their numbers */\n\t@media (0.50) and (width >= 1.50) and (1.50 < width < 2.50) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* a function call in name position is name text like anything else there — and its\n\tparens do not protect the splitting colon, so a name may run INTO a call and the value\n\tstart inside one */\n\t@media (calc(1.50): a) and (calc(1.50)) and (calc(1: 1.5): b) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* the colon that splits an expression is its first one wherever it sits, so a\n\tgrouped condition's value normalizes */\n\t@media (not (a: 1.5)) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* a comment is name text, and the name runs on past it to the colon */\n\t@media (1.50 /* c */: a) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* a `(` glued to an identifier is a function call in media-type position rather than\n\ta feature expression, so its content takes the number pass like the rest of the type */\n\t@media calc(1.5) and (calc(1.50): a) {\n\t\ta {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* @custom-media goes through the same reader */\n\t@custom-media --b (0.50);\n",
			"comment": null
		}
